{
  "id": "T-CHATSHOTS",
  "title": "DEV screenshot capture of the RESTYLED floating chat window (user-approved 2026-09-28, mock-ups C1-C4; folds U1-U3, R1-R14): default place BOTTOM RIGHT just left of the BizPhone (phone open, a game notice card top-right), empty; 40 LOCAL lines (two long wrapped ones, private ones - name in the player's colour, '(private)' purple - and a typed '<3 <b>not bold</b>' shown literally) with the newest fully visible; scrolled back with a new message arriving ('New messages' pill); the TO dropdown open; a small size; a moved + resized place that is REMEMBERED (close + reopen restores it, log-asserted); the HUD with the filled chat back at its default place. Then a Business Hub note to the client must arrive as a pop-up notice, not a chat line. Host + 1 client on save1. Sample lines are display-only (never sent, never saved) and cleared at the end; the remembered place is forgotten at the start and the end. Run at two sizes: normal, and BAMP_RIG_WINDOW=1280x720.",
  "preconditions": "Dev build with the chatview (open/close/size/scroll PX/drop/reset/place X Y W H/gamenotice/state) / uifill / hubnote levers (TestDrive.cs). Fixture save1 (host melaus, client Client1). Keep the host window unfocused but NOT minimised (a minimised window does not render).",
